Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; ============================================================================
;  Explorer right-click menu: "Compress + OCR this folder (in place)" on a
;  folder.
;
;  Double-click this file to install, then confirm the prompt. No admin rights
;  are needed: everything goes under HKEY_CURRENT_USER, which Explorer merges
;  into HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT for your account only. Log out/in or restart Explorer
;  if the entry does not appear immediately.
;
;  On Windows 11 the entry lives under "Show more options" (Shift+F10 opens
;  that menu directly).
;
;  WHAT IT DOES: runs the tool over the folder with default settings and
;  --in-place. Subfolders are always included -- pointing the tool at a folder
;  walks the whole tree. Each scanned PDF is OVERWRITTEN with its compressed,
;  searchable version; non-PDF files, the folder structure, born-digital PDFs
;  that cannot be improved, and files that are already optimal are left alone.
;  This is DESTRUCTIVE to the scans themselves, so the .cmd behind this entry
;  asks you to type YES before it starts.
;
;  No log: the command passes no --log, so nothing is written to disk except the
;  PDFs, and the run reports to the console window only. Add --log to the
;  command line below if you want a report kept (it lands in the current
;  folder), or --log "D:\some\dir" to place it -- never inside the manuals.
;
;  IF YOU MOVE THE REPO: change the one path below
;      S:\Projects\Home\ocrmyworkshopmanual\tools\compress_folder_here.cmd
;  (keep the doubled backslashes) and re-import. The .cmd finds the script and
;  the virtualenv relative to its own location, so nothing else needs editing.
;
;  To remove: run compress-folder-context-menu-uninstall.reg.
; ============================================================================

[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Classes\Directory\shell\CompressPDFFolder]
"MUIVerb"="Compress + OCR this folder (in place)"
"Icon"="shell32.dll,-16826"

[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Classes\Directory\shell\CompressPDFFolder\command]
@="\"S:\\Projects\\Home\\ocrmyworkshopmanual\\tools\\compress_folder_here.cmd\" \"%V\""
